Hoisting the `profile` pointer into a local and marking the invalid-range branch as unlikely lets the compiler keep the common path branch-free-ish and avoid a redundant load.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```